   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = 3 e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{3}} \\) and \\( g(x) = - \\frac{3 x}{2} \\). Let R be the region bounded by the graphs of f and g and the vertical lines \\( x = 0 \\) and \\( x = 2 \\). R is the base of a solid whose cross sections perpendicular to the x-axis are rectangles whose heights are 3 times their bases. Using a calculator, find the volume of the solid. Show the setup for the calculation, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
      "setup_required": true,
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 76.5170491837757,
      "decimals": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The base of each cross section is the vertical distance across R, \\( s = f(x) - g(x) = \\frac{3 x}{2} + 3 e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{3}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "distance between the boundary curves"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Because a rectangle with base s and height 3s has area 3s^2, each cross section has area \\( 3s^{2} \\).",
         "rule_named": "area of the named shape"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The volume is \\( \\int_{0}^{2} 3\\left(\\frac{3 x}{2} + 3 e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{3}}\\right)^{2}\\,dx \\), which a calculator gives as about 76.517.",
         "mathjson": 76.5170491837757,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "volume by cross sections"
      }
   ],
